From: Pad 2 bring-up <local@localhost>
Subject: [PATCH] power: supply: qcom_battmgr: validate Oplus property replies

Match replies to the pending opcode/property, validate lengths and report
firmware errors as negative errno values. Serialize notification enable with
other requests and protect pending state against timeout/receive races.
The wire protocol has no transaction ID: a late reply to an identical retried
request cannot be distinguished. SET reply values are not readback values.

Stop Oplus workers after failed requests and report their errors, preserving
the successful write sequence. Remove inherited commented-out experiments.
Drop SM8550 charge thresholds: Oplus property IDs 25/26 are PDO/QC controls,
and the generic 0x48 setter is unvalidated on this firmware. Reuse the
read-only SM8350 battery descriptor. X1E80100's separate interface remains.

--- a/drivers/power/supply/qcom_battmgr.c
+++ b/drivers/power/supply/qcom_battmgr.c
@@ -16,6 +16,7 @@
 #include <linux/soc/qcom/pmic_glink.h>
 #include <linux/math.h>
 #include <linux/units.h>
+#include <linux/spinlock.h>
 
 #define BATTMGR_CHEMISTRY_LEN	4
 #define BATTMGR_STRING_LEN	128
@@ -72,8 +73,6 @@
